# MkDocs Material Theme Customization

## Overview
This rule covers how to customize the Material for MkDocs theme using CSS, JavaScript, and theme extensions.

## Adding Assets

### Additional CSS
For small tweaks to colors, spacing, or element styling:

1. **Create CSS file structure:**
   ```
   docs/
   └─ stylesheets/
      └─ extra.css
   ```

2. **Add to mkdocs.yml:**
   ```yaml
   extra_css:
     - stylesheets/extra.css
   ```

### Additional JavaScript
For custom logic or third-party integrations:

1. **Create JavaScript file structure:**
   ```
   docs/
   └─ javascripts/
      └─ extra.js
   ```

2. **Add to mkdocs.yml:**
   ```yaml
   extra_javascript:
     - javascripts/extra.js
   ```

3. **Use document$ observable for page load events:**
   ```javascript
   document$.subscribe(function() {
     console.log("Initialize third-party libraries here")
   })
   ```

## Theme Extension

### Setup
For HTML source modifications (add/remove parts):

1. **Enable theme extension in mkdocs.yml:**
   ```yaml
   theme:
     name: material
     custom_dir: overrides
   ```

2. **Create overrides directory structure:**
   ```
   overrides/
   ├─ partials/
   │  ├─ footer.html
   │  ├─ header.html
   │  └─ ...
   ├─ main.html
   └─ base.html
   ```

### Overriding Partials
Replace any partial by creating a file with the same name and location:
- `overrides/partials/footer.html` replaces the original footer
- `overrides/partials/header.html` replaces the original header

### Overriding Blocks (Recommended)
Use `main.html` to override template blocks:

```html
{% extends "base.html" %}

{% block htmltitle %}
  <title>Custom Title</title>
{% endblock %}

{% block scripts %}
  <!-- Add scripts before -->
  {{ super() }}
  <!-- Add scripts after -->
{% endblock %}
```

### Available Template Blocks
| Block | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `analytics` | Google Analytics integration |
| `announce` | Announcement bar |
| `config` | JavaScript application config |
| `container` | Main content container |
| `content` | Main content |
| `extrahead` | Custom meta tags |
| `fonts` | Font definitions |
| `footer` | Footer with navigation |
| `header` | Fixed header bar |
| `hero` | Hero teaser |
| `htmltitle` | `<title>` tag |
| `libs` | JavaScript libraries (header) |
| `outdated` | Version warning |
| `scripts` | JavaScript application (footer) |
| `site_meta` | Meta tags in document head |
| `site_nav` | Site navigation and TOC |
| `styles` | Style sheets |
| `tabs` | Tabs navigation |

## Best Practices

### CSS Customization
- Use `!important` sparingly and only when necessary
- Target specific selectors for better specificity
- Test changes across different screen sizes
- Use CSS custom properties for theme colors

### JavaScript Integration
- Always use `document$.subscribe()` for page load events
- Handle instant loading properly (no page refresh)
- Test with and without instant loading enabled

### Theme Extension
- Mirror the original theme structure exactly
- Use `{{ super() }}` to extend rather than replace blocks
- Keep overrides minimal to ease theme updates

## Common Customizations

### Content Width
```css
.md-content__inner {
    max-width: none !important;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 1rem;
}
```

### Sidebar Adjustments
```css
.md-sidebar {
    width: 200px !important;
    padding: 0 0.5rem !important;
}

.md-sidebar--primary,
.md-sidebar--secondary {
    width: 200px !important;
}
```

### Color Scheme
```css
:root {
    --md-primary-fg-color: #your-color;
    --md-accent-fg-color: #your-accent;
}
```

### Navigation and TOC Customization

#### Overview
The Material theme provides comprehensive CSS classes to customize the navigation sidebar and table of contents (TOC) panes. You can make them more compact, reduce font sizes, and adjust spacing.

#### Navigation Sidebar Classes

**Main Navigation Container:**
```css
.md-nav {
  font-size: 12px; /* Default: 14px */
}

.md-nav__link {
  padding: 6px 8px; /* Default: 12px 16px */
  margin-top: 0.4em; /* Default: 0.625em */
}
```

**Primary Navigation (Desktop/Drawer):**
```css
.md-nav--primary .md-nav__title,
.md-nav--primary .md-nav__item {
  font-size: 14px; /* Default: 16px */
  line-height: 1.3; /* Default: 1.5 */
}

.md-nav--primary .md-nav__link {
  padding: 8px 12px; /* Default: 12px 16px */
}
```

**Navigation Icons:**
```css
.md-nav--primary .md-nav__icon {
  width: 18px; /* Default: 24px */
  height: 18px; /* Default: 24px */
  font-size: 18px; /* Default: typography/24px */
}
```

#### Sidebar Width & Spacing
```css
.md-sidebar {
  width: 200px; /* Default: 242px */
  padding: 12px 0; /* Default: 24px 0 */
}

.md-sidebar__scrollwrap {
  margin: 0 2px; /* Default: 0 4px */
}
```

#### Table of Contents (TOC) Classes

**TOC Navigation Container:**
```css
.md-nav--secondary {
  font-size: 12px; /* Inherits from .md-nav */
}

.md-nav--secondary .md-nav__list {
  padding-inline-start: 6px; /* Default: 12px */
  padding-bottom: 4px; /* Default: 8px */
}

.md-nav--secondary .md-nav__item > .md-nav__link {
  margin-inline-end: 4px; /* Default: 8px */
}
```

**Nested TOC Links (Level 2-6):**
```css
.md-nav--secondary .md-nav .md-nav__link {
  padding-inline-start: 14px; /* Default: 28px for level 3 */
}

.md-nav--secondary .md-nav .md-nav .md-nav__link {
  padding-inline-start: 20px; /* Default: 40px for level 4 */
}

.md-nav--secondary .md-nav .md-nav .md-nav .md-nav__link {
  padding-inline-start: 26px;
}

.md-nav--secondary .md-nav .md-nav .md-nav .md-nav .md-nav__link {
  padding-inline-start: 32px;
}
```

#### Tree-like Navigation (Desktop)
```css
.md-nav--primary .md-nav__list {
  padding-inline-start: 6px; /* Default: 12px */
  padding-bottom: 4px; /* Default: 8px */
}

.md-nav--primary .md-nav__item > .md-nav__link {
  margin-inline-end: 4px; /* Default: 8px */
}
```

#### Complete CSS Override Example

Add to `docs/stylesheets/extra.css`:

```css
/* Compact Navigation */
.md-nav {
  font-size: 12px;
}

.md-nav__link {
  padding: 6px 8px;
  margin-top: 0.4em;
}

/* Compact Primary Navigation */
.md-nav--primary .md-nav__title,
.md-nav--primary .md-nav__item {
  font-size: 14px;
  line-height: 1.3;
}

.md-nav--primary .md-nav__link {
  padding: 8px 12px;
}

.md-nav--primary .md-nav__icon {
  width: 18px;
  height: 18px;
  font-size: 18px;
}

/* Compact Sidebar */
.md-sidebar {
  width: 200px;
  padding: 12px 0;
}

.md-sidebar__scrollwrap {
  margin: 0 2px;
}

/* Compact TOC */
.md-nav--secondary .md-nav__list {
  padding-inline-start: 6px;
  padding-bottom: 4px;
}

.md-nav--secondary .md-nav__item > .md-nav__link {
  margin-inline-end: 4px;
}

/* Reduce nested TOC indentation */
.md-nav--secondary .md-nav .md-nav__link {
  padding-inline-start: 14px;
}

.md-nav--secondary .md-nav .md-nav .md-nav__link {
  padding-inline-start: 20px;
}

.md-nav--secondary .md-nav .md-nav .md-nav .md-nav__link {
  padding-inline-start: 26px;
}

.md-nav--secondary .md-nav .md-nav .md-nav .md-nav .md-nav__link {
  padding-inline-start: 32px;
}

/* Tree-like Navigation */
.md-nav--primary .md-nav__list {
  padding-inline-start: 6px;
  padding-bottom: 4px;
}

.md-nav--primary .md-nav__item > .md-nav__link {
  margin-inline-end: 4px;
}
```

Configure in `mkdocs.yml`:
```yaml
extra_css:
  - stylesheets/extra.css
```

This configuration makes both the navigation sidebar and table of contents more compact with smaller fonts and reduced spacing while maintaining the theme's functionality and accessibility.

## Development Workflow

1. **Make changes** to CSS/JS files in `docs/`
2. **Test locally** with `uv run mkdocs serve --dev-addr=127.0.0.1:8001`
3. **Check browser console** for any JavaScript errors
4. **Validate** changes work across different pages
5. **Build** with `uv run mkdocs build` to check for errors
6. **Deploy** when ready

## Troubleshooting

### CSS Not Loading
- Check `extra_css` path in `mkdocs.yml`
- Verify file exists in correct location
- Restart MkDocs server after changes
- Check browser network tab for 404 errors

### JavaScript Issues
- Use `document$.subscribe()` for page events
- Check browser console for errors
- Test with instant loading disabled

### Theme Extension Problems
- Ensure `custom_dir` points to correct directory
- Verify file structure matches original theme
- Check for syntax errors in HTML templates
- Use `{{ super() }}` when extending blocks

